  Film photo, Kodak 400 Portra film, natural colors, raw unedited aesthetic, shallow depth of field,  skin pores visible, no retouching, 8K resolution, documentary realism,
  Film photo, kodak 400 portra film, natural colors, real life aesthetic, no retouching or artificial enhancement, candid moment, spontaneous composition, sharp focus, fine details, 8k, depth of field, very high quality photo, very detailed photo, natural lighting, skin imperfections, skin blemishes, skin pores, without makeup. 
  ((Candid street photography, shot on 35mm film, slight grain, natural skin texture, imperfect lighting)),
  Midjourney-style documentary shot, Kodak Ektachrome 100 film,
  high-definition authentic candid photograph, realistic style, natural lighting, everyday imperfect people with genuine flaws, neutral expressions, shallow depth of field, raw candid moment,  documentary realism, , true-to-life skin textures including pores and blemishes, spontaneous composition,  environmental context suggesting mundane reality, captured on 35mm film with subtle grain, no retouching or artificial enhancement, true-to-life color grading, imperfect framing, authentic snapshot feel,
  A documentary street photograph in the style of Magnum Photos, shot on a Leica M6 with a Summicron 35mm lens. High contrast environmental lighting, gritty realism, and authentic human presence. The subject is an average person. The skin shows signs of weather exposure, natural aging, and realistic texture. Composition is candid and spontaneous, capturing a raw moment of everyday life with uncompromising photographic honesty,
  Editorial fashion photography, shot on Hasselblad, medium format film look, high contrast, detailed fabric texture, 
  Golden-hour film still, 35mm Fuji Pro 400H, shallow depth of field,
  Ultra high fidelity documentary photography shot on medium format film with zero digital postprocessing. The image exhibits all the imperfections of real analog capture slight emulsion grain, subtle light leaks from the camera back, and natural optical vignetting from vintage lenses. Skin tones retain their authentic variations, with visible pores, fine hairs, and uneven pigmentation rendered in meticulous detail. Shadows contain true film grain structure, not artificial noise. Highlights roll off organically into blown out areas without harsh clipping. The composition has the accidental cropping and awkward framing of a real photographer’s rushed snap, not the perfect symmetry of CGI. Every element from fabric wrinkles to stray hairs obeys real world physics in how it interacts with light and depth of field.
  early-2000s candid film snapshot aesthetic with medium analog grain and visible flash bloom.
  (mirror selfie, taken on a 2003 digital camera, harsh direct flash, slight motion blur, has smudges and dust particles.)
